Patch 14 -- p70b symmetric A/B for draw-state phase A.

Incremental after patch 13 and Wine patch 68. Entry 40's wrapper registers the
guest-side selector from the argument object on its first routed call and then
reads the arm from it, exactly as entry 38 does. Once registered, guest x86
calls this bridge only for the routed arm and calls the phase-A transaction body
directly for the control arm, so neither arm pays a RunFunctionFmt() re-entry.

`mgs2_island_ab.c` previously hard-coded entry 38 in both the registration and
the selector test. Those two places now share one `mgs2_ab_guest_capable()`
predicate listing the entries that ship a guest-side selector, and the
registration log line names the entry instead of asserting 38. Everything else
in the A/B harness -- ABBA blocks, discarded settle frames, per-cycle pairing,
displayed-frame tick and cumulative counters -- is unchanged.

The memory-only phase-A record from patch 13 stays armed: it counts routed calls
and guest fallbacks without writing to stderr, so it does not disqualify the run
for timing. Build without MGS2_ISLAND_DIAGNOSTICS; regenerate the entry identity
and class-B table from the exact paired DLL. This patch makes no frame-rate
claim.

